build_libqemu-esp32.sh: build the library with pixman

The script disables every optional QEMU feature before enabling the few it
needs. That includes pixman, without which QEMU stubs out display
surfaces: the virtual RGB panel (esp_rgb) shows nothing and QMP has no
screendump. Enable it.

Applied by esp32bench (core/crates/sim/src/lcgamboa.rs) to lcgamboa/qemu
at 885a6e7061fb70fac78a074a719423810bc19a17.

diff --git a/build_libqemu-esp32.sh b/build_libqemu-esp32.sh
index 8d51e51..969e6bb 100755
--- a/build_libqemu-esp32.sh
+++ b/build_libqemu-esp32.sh
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ flags="$(./configure --help | perl -ne 'print if s/^  ([a-z][\w-]*) .*/\1/' | ta
 ${2:-.}/configure --target-list=$target --extra-cflags=-fPIC --disable-slirp $flags --enable-tcg \
 	--enable-system --disable-werror --disable-alsa  \
         --enable-debug --enable-debug-info \
-        --enable-gcrypt --enable-slirp 
+        --enable-gcrypt --enable-slirp --enable-pixman 
 	#--enable-gtk
 
 make clean >/dev/null
